WEBVTT

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:33.110
but it means if you're relying
entirely on this fluid intelligence,

00:06:33.134 --> 00:06:34.524
you're going to struggle.

00:06:34.548 --> 00:06:36.364
AG: A common refrain in Silicon Valley

00:06:36.388 --> 00:06:38.729
is that young people are just smarter.

00:06:38.753 --> 00:06:41.975
When it comes to fluid intelligence,
that's generally true.

00:06:41.999 --> 00:06:45.110
But the story changes
with crystallized intelligence,

00:06:45.134 --> 00:06:47.165
your acquired ability to solve problems

00:06:47.189 --> 00:06:49.355
by applying your knowledge and experience.

00:06:49.379 --> 00:06:51.260
AB: Your ability to synthesize things

00:06:51.284 --> 00:06:54.242
that you didn't necessarily invent,

00:06:54.266 --> 00:06:55.814
that's crystallized intelligence

00:06:55.838 --> 00:06:57.361
and that tends to happen later.

00:06:57.385 --> 00:06:59.306
(Music)

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:02.782
AG: Think about how crystallized
intelligence comes in handy in your job.